<title>PHILIPPINES: Asian Terminals buys into port firm.</title>
<headline>Asian Terminals buys into port firm.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Asian Terminals Inc of the Philippines said on Tuesday it had signed a shareholders' agreement with a local cargo handling firm for a 60 percent buy-in.</p>
<p>The port operator told the Philippine Stock Exchange it would buy into Aries Arrastre Services Inc, a firm with an authorised capital of four million pesos.</p>
<p>Details of the buy-in were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Aries is a company based in the port city of Batangas, just south of Manila.</p>
<p>-- Manila Newsroom (63 2) 841-8938 Fax 817-6267</p>
